{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CosineParametrisationUnfalsifiable","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CosineParametrisationUnfalsifiable","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Trigonometric"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cos_parametrisation_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cos_parametrisation_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CosineParametrisationUnfalsifiable.lean#L94-L114","doc":"**The cosine parametrisation is 2-to-1.** Because `cos` is even, the two\nMarkov parameters `z₁ ≠ z₂` symmetric about `1 + u/h` give the *same* N=1\ncorrection. The exact correction is affine in `z` (`traceDelta_cross_mul`) hence\ninjective, so passing to the cosine discards a distinction the underlying object\nmakes — the algebraic form of the branch ambiguity the corpus met as a\n\"square-root branch point 0.062 % above q₀\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ck_residual_dominates_cos_departure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ck_residual_dominates_cos_departure","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CosineParametrisationUnfalsifiable.lean#L81-L92","doc":"**The `c_k` residual dominates it by two orders of magnitude.** With the\nphysical phase and the measured residual `r ≥ 7e-5` that the ladder must absorb,\nthe cosine's entire signature is at most `r/100`.\n\nThis is the file's point: the `c_k` tower is not correcting a cosine, it is\ncorrecting a quadratic — and it would be the same tower for any function with\nthe same second-order behaviour. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cos_departure_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cos_departure_le","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CosineParametrisationUnfalsifiable.lean#L67-L79","doc":"**The cosine's own signature is tiny on the physical phase.** For\n`|θ| ≤ 3/50` — which covers the measured `|θ| = 0.0566` (convention C) and\n`0.0447` (convention D) — the departure of `cos θ` from its quadratic truncation\nis at most `7e-7`, i.e. below the `7.784e-7` one-sigma resolution of the measured\n`Q_β/Q_A`. Everything that makes a cosine a cosine is invisible here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}